ncit:C102656 a cfa:NCItConcept ;
    skos:definition "A microbial identification technique in which polymerase chain reaction is used to amplify specific nucleic acid sequences in a biospecimen. The product of this reaction is then applied to a nitrocellulose test strip containing complementary DNA probes." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Line Probe Assay" .

