ncit:C28408 a cfa:NCItConcept ;
    skos:altLabel "Quantitative RTPCR",
        "qRTPCR" ;
    skos:definition "A modified polymerase chain reaction (PCR) technique in which RNA sequences are reverse transcribed into complementary DNA (cDNA) transcripts by the enzyme reverse transcriptase. The cDNA is then amplified by a real time PCR reaction. The level of expression of a target gene is calculated using the crossing thresholds (CTs) or crossing points (CPs) which correspond to the numbers of cycles required for a target gene and the housekeeping, internal control gene, to reach a defined fluorescence intensity." ;
    skos:prefLabel "Quantitative Reverse Transcriptase PCR" .

ncit:C33839 a cfa:NCItConcept ;
