var:MB-MBCAT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "MBCAT" ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:MB .

var:MB-MBMETHOD a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "MBMETHOD" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:MB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Interpretation_Context ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Interpretation_Context in Domain_Behaviour: COSMoS has MBMETHOD on 14 of 14 MB DSSs (assigned on 6, value list on 1, no value on 7; COSMoS_Use mixed); it never separates the DSSs of one BC (not in Variable_Evidence); codelist METHOD (C85492). SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Exp. SDTM v2.0: Record Qualifier. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Method of the test or examination. Examples: \"GRAM STAIN\", \"MICROBIAL CULTURE, LIQUID\", \"QUANTITATIVE REVERSE TRANSCRIPTASE POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION\".' LBMETHOD, GFMETHOD and ISMETHOD are method from COSMoS fan-out (Variable_Evidence in Domain_Behaviour); no source separates MB DSSs by method. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Kind: observable — the method of the test (as --METHOD in LB, GF, IS, and EGMETHOD); Position open until a source says more." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:MI-MIMETHOD a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "MIMETHOD" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:MI ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Interpretation_Context ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Interpretation_Context in Domain_Behaviour: COSMoS has MIMETHOD on 7 of 8 MI DSSs (assigned on 7; COSMoS_Use always assigned); it never separates the DSSs of one BC (not in Variable_Evidence); codelist METHOD (C85492). SDTMIG v3.4 Record Qualifier, Perm. SDTM v2.0: Record Qualifier. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Method of the test or examination. This could include the technique or type of staining used for the slides. Examples: \"IHC\", \"Crystal violet\", \"Safranin\", \"Trypan blue\", or \"Propidium iodide\".' LBMETHOD, GFMETHOD and ISMETHOD are method from COSMoS fan-out (Variable_Evidence in Domain_Behaviour); no source separates MI DSSs by method. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Kind: observable — the method of the test (as --METHOD in LB, GF, IS, and EGMETHOD); Position open until a source says more." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:MI-MITSTDTL a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "MITSTDTL" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:Component ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:MI ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Variable_Evidence ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources disagree, decided by a stated rule" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: SPECIFIES, \"further describes the test in\", codelist MIFTSDTL. SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --TESTCD, like the other --TSTDTL rows. SDTMIG v3.4 MI: Record Qualifier; MI Assumption 2: 'MITSTDTL further qualifies the record' — the IG prose matches its own role; its examples are 'H SCORE TOTAL SCORE', 'STAINING INTENSITY', 'PERCENT POSITIVE CELL'. The sources differ on role, not on the observable: the SDTM roles do not separate identifying qualifiers from subject state (--SPEC and --METHOD are Record Qualifiers too; Variable_Evidence in Domain_Behaviour). Rule (2026-10-08): the role does not decide; a separate SDTM CT term with its own NCIt code is a separate component (the LBTESTCD rule). The assigned MITSTDTL values are MIFTSDTL terms with their own NCIt codes. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Further description of the test performed in producing the MI result. This would be used to represent specific attributes, such as intensity score or percentage of cells displaying presence of the biomarker or compound.' In COSMoS MITSTDTL is the only assigned value that separates the DSSs of one BC (Allred proportion positive score, staining intensity score and total score, for the estrogen and for the progesterone receptor); all are integer without units, so scale does not separate them. Two readings: the test detail narrows what is measured (component), or it names the kind of quantity reported (a property, in LOINC's terms). Both keep the DSSs apart, unlike ISTSTDTL, where the score systems go with a change of scale. The key has no property part, so it is carried as component. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: MI-A2, MITSTDTL-Notes. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

