var:LB-LBSTRESU a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBSTRESU" ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB .

var:LB-LBORRESU a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBORRESU" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:OpenFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Interpretation_Context ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "Interpretation_Context in Domain_Behaviour: COSMoS has LBORRESU on 117 of 147 LB DSSs (assigned on 14, value list on 102, no value on 1; COSMoS_Use mixed); it never separates the DSSs of one BC (not in Variable_Evidence); codelist UNIT (C71620). SDTMIG v3.4 Variable Qualifier, Exp. SDTM v2.0: Variable Qualifier of --ORRES, --ORNRLO, --ORNRHI, --ORREF; NCIt concept of --ORRESU: Original Result Unit. SDTMIG v3.4 CDISC Notes: 'Original units in which the data were collected. The unit for LBORRES. Example: \"g/L\".' SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBORRESU is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. The Model ties the unit to the result, LB-A8 to the test. No source says whether this variable is part of the observable. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: open — a planned unit names the property of the observable (docs/Observables_Direction.md); a reported unit is the form of the result. The key has no property part." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "proposed" .

var:LB-LBFAST a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBFAST" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:PracticeFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-LOINC_Subject_State ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: LBFAST is a value list (N;Y), never assigned, so it never separates sibling DSSs and is not in Variable_Evidence. LOINC (Subject_State in COSMoS_Observable_LOINC_Check): fasting-free and fasting-qualified glucose codes side by side (component Glucose^post CFst, class CHAL). LOINC offers fasting as a refinement, not as a requirement; no source says whether fasting is part of the observable. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Record Qualifier, like --SPEC and --METHOD; no published role separates subject state from identifying qualifiers. SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: LBFAST is among 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code', 'only required to be populated when necessary to provide a semantically meaningful distinction between records with different LBLOINC values'. COSMoS, LOINC and the IG agree that subject state is an optional refinement; none says it is always or never part of the observable (decided 2026-10-08: open, the conditional reading carried into Phase 2). Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: practice — fasting is a condition on the subject, set by how the observation is brought about (COSMoS and LOINC: subject state)." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

ncit:C49487 a cfa:NCItConcept ;
    skos:definition "The non-affirmative response to a question. (NCI)" ;
    skos:prefLabel "No" .

ncit:C49488 a cfa:NCItConcept ;
    skos:definition "The affirmative response to a question. (NCI)" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yes" .

cl:C66742 a cfa:Codelist ;
    rdfs:label "No Yes Response" ;
    skos:notation "NY" ;
    cfa:extensible false ;
    cfa:isIdentifiedBy ncit:C66742 .

var:LB-LBCAT a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBCAT" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:RecordFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:OpenPosition ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Variable_Evidence ;
    cfa:positionBasis "standards silent, open" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: predicate GROUPS, \"groups values in\"; DEC not stated. No codelist; values without NCIt code. LBCAT and LOINC class are different groupings (LBCAT_LOINC_Class in Domain_Behaviour). No source says whether category changes the observation. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Grouping Qualifier. Kind: record — groups the records; carried, not keyed." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

var:LB-LBSPEC a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBSPEC" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:System ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Variable_Evidence ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources agree" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS: predicate IS_SPECIMEN_TESTED_IN, \"is the specimen tested in\", codelist SPECTYPE. Fan-out axis specimen and key part system agree (Key_Compare in Domain_Behaviour). LOINC system agrees (LOINC_Compare in Domain_Behaviour); the exceptions are COSMoS pin errors reported by COSMoS_Observable_LOINC_Check. SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Record Qualifier, the same role as --POS and --FAST; the role does not separate them. SDTMIG v3.4 LB Assumption 8: with LBTEST and LBORRESU, 'the aspects of a test that are associated with a LOINC code'. Quoted in SDTMIG_Statements.xlsx: LB-A8. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

var:LB-LBTESTCD a cfa:Variable ;
    skos:notation "LBTESTCD" ;
    cfa:facetKind cfa:ObservableFacet ;
    cfa:facetPosition cfa:Component ;
    cfa:inDomain dom:LB ;
    cfa:isEvidencedBy val:keysource-Variable_Evidence ;
    cfa:positionBasis "sources disagree, decided by a stated rule" ;
    cfa:positionBasisNote "COSMoS puts GLUC and GLUCPE under one BC (C105585). SDTM CT publishes them as separate LBTESTCD terms with their own NCIt codes and definitions (GLUC C105585; GLUCPE C163446, \"plasma equivalent glucose\"). The key separates them; the fan-out does not. Rule (adopted 2026-10-08): a separate SDTM CT test term with its own NCIt code is a separate component (identity keyed on NCIt codes, Observables_Direction step 2). SDTM v2.0 and SDTMIG v3.4: Topic. Kind: observable — follows from the position." ;
    cfa:positionStatus "accepted" .

